course: dictionary
lesson: 7335
title: Plant: a living thing, a factory, or an action
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. A plant is usually a living thing that grows in soil. «When we burn them we release sunlight that ancient plants caught long before the dinosaurs.» Here plants are living things, because they caught sunlight.
explain: Now look at «In 1986 a reactor at the Chornobyl power plant in Ukraine exploded and spread radiation.» A power plant is not a living thing. It is a factory or big machine. Ask yourself: does the meaning fit the sentence? A factory fits here, so that is the meaning.
explain: Plant can also be a verb, a doing word. To plant means to put seeds or plants in the ground so they grow. «She planted her feet» means something different: it means she put her feet firmly in place. Always check your meaning by swapping it back into the sentence.
fact: A plant is a living thing that grows in soil, like a flower, grass or a tree.
fact: Most plants are green and make their own food from sunlight.
fact: To plant means to put seeds or plants in the ground so they grow.
fact: A power plant is a factory or big machine that makes power.
fact: «Planted» can also mean put firmly in place, as in «she planted her feet».
exercise: Most plants are green and make their own food from sunlight. What is a plant? | A bird that eats seeds | A machine that makes power | A kind of rock | *A living thing that grows in soil
exercise: «When we burn them we release sunlight that ancient plants caught long before the dinosaurs.» What does plants mean in this sentence? | Seeds put into the ground | Factories that make power | *Living things that grow in soil | Ways of standing firm
exercise: «In 1986 a reactor at the Chornobyl power plant in Ukraine exploded.» What does power plant mean? | A place where people sleep | *A factory or big machine that makes power | A plant that grows in a pot | A garden full of flowers
test: «She planted her feet and would not move.» What does planted mean here? | Dug a hole and put seeds in the ground | *Put firmly in place | Grew tall like a tree | Hid under a stone
test: The children planted beans in rows in the school garden. What does planted mean? | *Put seeds in the ground so they grow | Hid them under a stone | Stood very still | Counted them in a sum
exam: «Seeds must travel away from their parent, so the young plants do not compete with it for light and water.» What do young plants need that they must not fight their parent for? | Feathers and fur | *Light and water | Sand and rocks | Parachutes and burrs
